.TH DARPA_SPILL_CLIENT 3 "September 24, 2026" "darpa_spillserver 1.3.0" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
darpa_spill_client \- C and C++ client library for the DARPA Spill Information Server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <darpa_spill/client.hpp>
.B #include <darpa_spill/config.hpp>
.B #include <darpa_spill/format.hpp>
.PP
.B #include <darpa_spill/client.h>
.PP
Link with \fB\-ldarpa_spill_client \-lboost_json\fR, or in CMake:
.PP
.B find_package(DarpaSpillClient 1.3 REQUIRED)
.B target_link_libraries(prog PRIVATE DarpaSpill::client)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B libdarpa_spill_client
talks to the HTTP API of a
.BR darpa-spill-server (1),
which serves NOvA accelerator event timestamps recorded from a TDU. It is a
synchronous HTTP/1.1 client built on Boost.Beast: each call opens one
connection, sends one request and reads the whole response. The export route
is the exception, and is streamed to a
.B std::ostream
in constant memory. The server sends its query results with chunked transfer
encoding, and the library decodes it.
.PP
The parameters each call sends, their order, the percent-encoding and the way
error bodies are decoded are fixed by
.I docs/CLIENT.md
and shared with the Python client
.BR darpa_spillserver (3).
.BR darpa-spill-client-cpp (1)
is built on this library.
.PP
The C++ interface lives in namespace
.BR darpa::spill .
Parsed responses are
.BR boost::json::value s,
so Boost.JSON is a public dependency. yaml-cpp, OpenSSL and the rest of Boost
are used only inside the library.
.SH C++ INTERFACE
.SS Connection options
.nf
.B struct ClientOptions {
.B "    std::string url = \(dqhttp://localhost:8080\(dq;"
.B "    double timeout = 30.0;"
.B "    std::string admin_token;"
.B "    std::string ca_file;"
.B "    bool verify_tls = true;"
.B };
.fi
.PP
.I url
may carry a path prefix, such as
.BR https://gateway/spills ,
when the server runs behind a proxy.
.I timeout
applies to each network operation (resolve, connect, handshake, write and
every read) separately.
.I admin_token
is sent as the
.B X\-Admin\-Token
header when it is not empty.
.I ca_file
names a PEM bundle; when it is empty the system store is used.
.SS Selections
.nf
.B struct Selection {
.B "    std::optional<std::string> start, end;"
.B "    std::vector<std::string> signals, types, sources;"
.B "    std::optional<std::string> tz, columns;"
.B };
.B struct Paging {
.B "    std::optional<std::int64_t> limit, offset;"
.B "    bool descending = false;"
.B };
.B enum class Format { json, csv };
.fi
.PP
Times are any expression the server accepts
.RB ( now ", " today ", " \-2h ", " 2026\-07\-01T09:15:00Z ", " nova: \fITICKS\fR);
see
.BR "Client::time_help" .
Repeated signals, types and sources form a union.
.SS The client
.nf
.B "explicit Client(ClientOptions options);"
.PP
.B "boost::json::value health() const;"
.B "boost::json::value status() const;"
.B "boost::json::value sources() const;"
.B "boost::json::value signals() const;"
.B "boost::json::value types() const;"
.B "boost::json::value time_convert(const std::string& t,"
.B "                                const std::optional<std::string>& tz = {}) const;"
.B "boost::json::value time_help() const;"
.B "boost::json::value latest(const std::optional<std::string>& signal = {},"
.B "                          const std::vector<std::string>& sources = {}) const;"
.B "boost::json::value events(const Selection&, const Paging& = {}) const;"
.B "std::string        events_csv(const Selection&, const Paging& = {}) const;"
.B "void               export_to(const Selection&, std::ostream& out,"
.B "                             Format format = Format::csv) const;"
.B "boost::json::value admin_check() const;"
.B "boost::json::value update_source(const std::string& name,"
.B "                                 std::optional<bool> enabled,"
.B "                                 std::optional<std::string> base_url) const;"
.B "boost::json::value reset_source(const std::string& name) const;"
.fi
.PP
Each method maps to one route under
.IR /api ;
.BR darpa-spill-client (1)
lists them. The constructor rejects a URL that is not
.B http://
or
.BR https:// .
The client holds no connection between calls, and a
.B const
client may be used from several threads at once.
.SS Raw access
.nf
.B "Response request(const std::string& method, const std::string& path,"
.B "                 const Params& params = {}, const std::string& json_body = {}) const;"
.B "Response checked(...same arguments...) const;"
.B "void     stream(const std::string& path, const Params& params, std::ostream& out) const;"
.PP
.B "struct Response { int status; std::string reason, content_type, body; };"
.B "using Params = std::vector<std::pair<std::string, std::string>>;"
.fi
.PP
.B request
returns the response whatever its status.
.B checked
throws
.B HttpError
for a status of 400 or above.
.B stream
writes the body to
.I out
as it arrives, and throws before writing anything if the status is an error.
.SS Helpers
.TP
.B "std::string percent_encode(const std::string&)"
RFC 3986 encoding: only
.B "A\-Z a\-z 0\-9 \- . _ ~"
pass through, so
.B $74
becomes
.BR %2474 .
.TP
.B "std::string build_query(const Params&)"
Encode parameters as \fBk=v&k=v\fR, keeping their order.
.TP
.B "Params selection_params(const Selection&, std::optional<Format>, const Paging* = nullptr)"
The parameters of
.I /api/events
and
.IR /api/export ,
in the fixed order \fBstart end signal type source format limit offset order
tz columns\fR.
.TP
.B "const char* version()"
The library version, for example \fB1.3.0\fR.
.SS Configuration
.B darpa_spill/config.hpp
provides the client configuration used by the command line:
.B load_config(const LoadRequest&)
merges the defaults, a YAML file, a \fB.env\fR file, the environment and
command-line overrides, highest last, into a
.BR ClientConfig .
.B ClientConfig::to_options()
turns the result into
.BR ClientOptions ,
reading
.I admin_token_file
if that is set. It throws
.B ConfigError
on a missing file, an unknown key or a bad value. The keys, variables and
files are described in
.BR darpa-spill-client (1).
.SS Rendering
.B darpa_spill/format.hpp
exposes the command line's output rules:
.BR format_cell ,
.BR render_table ,
.BR render_csv ,
.BR parse_csv ,
.BR flatten ,
.B render_kv
and
.BR split_csv_comments .
Use them to print responses exactly as the command-line clients do.
.SS Errors
.nf
.B "class Error           : public std::runtime_error;"
.B "class ConnectionError : public Error;   // DNS, connect, TLS, timeout"
.B "class HttpError       : public Error;   // status >= 400"
.B "    int status() const;"
.B "    const std::string& message() const;"
.B "    const std::string& hint() const;"
.B "    const std::string& body() const;"
.fi
.PP
.B ConnectionError::what()
reads \fBcannot reach \fIURL\fB: \fIreason\fR.
.B HttpError
takes its message and hint from the server's
.B {"detail": {"error": ..., "hint": ...}}
body. It also accepts a top-level
.BR {"error": ...} ,
a string
.BR detail ,
and FastAPI's validation list, whose first item becomes
.IB loc.path ": " msg\fR.
If none of these is present, the message is the HTTP reason phrase.
.SH C INTERFACE
.nf
.B "typedef struct dsc_client dsc_client;"
.PP
.BI "dsc_client *dsc_client_new(const char *" url ", double " timeout );
.BI "void dsc_client_free(dsc_client *" client );
.BI "int dsc_client_set_admin_token(dsc_client *" client ", const char *" token );
.BI "int dsc_client_set_tls(dsc_client *" client ", const char *" ca_file ", int " verify );
.BI "int dsc_get(dsc_client *" client ", const char *" path_and_query ,
.BI "            char **" body ", long *" status );
.BI "int dsc_request(dsc_client *" client ", const char *" method ,
.BI "                const char *" path_and_query ", const char *" json_body ,
.BI "                char **" body ", long *" status );
.BI "const char *dsc_last_error(const dsc_client *" client );
.BI "char *dsc_percent_encode(const char *" text );
.BI "void dsc_string_free(char *" text );
.B "const char *dsc_version(void);"
.fi
.PP
No function throws.
.B dsc_client_new
returns NULL if
.I url
is NULL or not an http or https URL; a
.I timeout
of zero or less means 30 seconds.
.I path_and_query
must start with
.B /
and carry its query string already encoded (use
.BR dsc_percent_encode ).
On
.B DSC_OK
and
.BR DSC_ERR_HTTP ,
.I *body
receives the response body, which the caller releases with
.BR dsc_string_free ,
and
.I *status
receives the HTTP status. Either pointer may be NULL.
.B dsc_last_error
describes the last failure on a client. The string is valid until the next
call on that client.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The C functions that return
.B int
return one of these codes. They match the exit status of the command-line
clients:
.TP
.B DSC_OK (0)
Success; the HTTP status is below 400.
.TP
.B DSC_ERR_HTTP (1)
The server answered with a status of 400 or above.
.TP
.B DSC_ERR_USAGE (2)
A NULL or malformed argument.
.TP
.B DSC_ERR_CONNECTION (3)
Connect, TLS or timeout failure.
.TP
.B DSC_ERR_INTERNAL (4)
Anything else, such as memory exhaustion.
.SH EXAMPLES
C++: today's NuMI spills as JSON, then a day of 1 Hz events streamed to a file.
.PP
.RS
.EX
#include <darpa_spill/client.hpp>
#include <fstream>
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    darpa::spill::ClientOptions options;
    options.url = "http://novadaq\-near\-gateway\-01.fnal.gov:8080";
    darpa::spill::Client client(options);

    darpa::spill::Selection numi;
    numi.start = "today";
    numi.signals = {"$74"};
    try {
        auto page = client.events(numi, darpa::spill::Paging{100, {}, false});
        std::cout << page.as_object().at("meta").as_object().at("total")
                  << " spills\en";

        darpa::spill::Selection hz;
        hz.start = hz.end = "2026\-07\-01";
        hz.signals = {"$8f"};
        std::ofstream out("one\-hertz.csv", std::ios::binary);
        client.export_to(hz, out);
    } catch (const darpa::spill::HttpError& e) {
        std::cerr << e.what() << "\en" << e.hint() << "\en";
        return 1;
    } catch (const darpa::spill::Error& e) {
        std::cerr << e.what() << "\en";
        return 3;
    }
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
C: the newest event (from
.I examples/c/latest.c
in the source distribution).
.PP
.RS
.EX
#include <darpa_spill/client.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
    dsc_client *c = dsc_client_new("http://localhost:8080", 30.0);
    char *body = NULL;
    long status = 0;
    int rc = dsc_get(c, "/api/latest?signal=%2474", &body, &status);
    if (rc == DSC_OK)
        puts(body);
    else
        fprintf(stderr, "%s\en", dsc_last_error(c));
    dsc_string_free(body);
    dsc_client_free(c);
    return rc;
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Build and link against an installed copy:
.PP
.RS
.EX
cc latest.c $(pkg\-config \-\-cflags \-\-libs darpa_spill_client) \-o latest
.EE
.RE
